      "text": "Hal changes the batteries every 5 months. To find the month he will change them the 25th time, we need to calculate 24 intervals (since the first change is in May). Because there are 4 months in a year, each interval means two months have passed (since there are 12 months in a year). If 24 intervals mean 48 months have passed, and every 5 months is 1 interval, we divide 48 by 5 to find how many years and months have elapsed. There are 9 full years and 3 months left after dividing 48 by 5. Therefore, we have \\(9 \\times 12 + 3 = 108 + 3 = 111\\) months from May.\n\nThus, Hal will change the batteries for the 25th time in \\(\\boxed{\\text{March 2021}}\\).",
